+# Matches a 16-digit credit card number written as four groups of four digits
+# with either no separator, a single space between groups or a single hyphen
+# between groups. The separator must be the same throughout, so mixed forms
+# such as "1234-5678 9012-3456" do not match. Written as three alternatives
+# rather than with a back-reference, which the regex engines used for
+# structured generation do not support. Like the ISBN below, this checks the
+# shape only, not the Luhn check digit.
+credit_card = Regex(
+    r"[0-9]{16}|[0-9]{4}( [0-9]{4}){3}|[0-9]{4}(-[0-9]{4}){3}"
+)
+
 # Matches any ISBN number. Note that this is not completely correct as not all
 # 10 or 13 digits numbers are valid ISBNs. See https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN
 # Taken from O'Reilly's Regular Expression Cookbook:
@@ -68,3 +79,8 @@ email = Regex(
